})();</script></div></div></div><div class="KLEmSd"></div><div data-encoded-docid="6e7tqGpESzOntFGiAAAAAA==" data-implicit-notification-eligible="false" data-result-index="0" data-title="Senior Data Scientist - IT Operations &amp; Analytics" role="group" jscontroller="leJiCf" jsdata="ZSBYQe;_;INP6aqDbJqqQ4-EPq6ieeQ50 xQKg9c;_;INP6aqDbJqqQ4-EPq6ieeQ53" jsaction="rcuQ6b:npT2md"><div><div class="XFOJCe"><h2 class="HKvozf IFnjPb">Job description</h2><span jsname="QAWWu" class="OOyDTc">Senior Data Scientist - IT Operations &amp; Analytics<br><br>Company: Atos<br>Job Location: Pune, Maharashtra, India<br>Employment Type: Full-time<br>Experience Required: 3+ years<br><br>About Atos Group<br><br>Atos Group is a global leader in digital transformation with c. 67,000 employees and annual revenue of c. 10 billion, operating in 61 countries under two brands Atos for services and Eviden for products. European number </span><span jsname="pqRzIf">...</span><span jsname="ij8cu" class="ejCXj" id="tsuid_INP6aqDbJqqQ4-EPq6ieeQ_222" aria-live="polite" style="display:none">one in cybersecurity, cloud and high performance computing, Atos Group is committed to a secure and decarbonized future and provides tailored AI-powered, end-to-end solutions for all industries. Atos Group is the brand under which Atos SE (Societas Europaea) operates. Atos SE is listed on Euronext Paris.<br><br>The purpose of Atos Group is to help design the future of the information space. Its expertise and services support the development of knowledge, education and research in a multicultural approach and contribute to the development of scientific and technological excellence. Across the world, the Group enables its customers and employees, and members of societies at large to live, work and develop sustainably, in a safe and secure information space.<br><br>Hiring for DataScientist Role<br><br>Role Overview:<br><br>Were seeking a highly skilled and self-directed Senior Data Scientist to lead complex analytics initiatives across IT operations, ITSM platforms, and telemetry systems. This role demands deep technical expertise, strategic thinking, and the ability to translate raw data into actionable insights that drive operational efficiency, user satisfaction, and business value.<br><br>Key Responsibilities:<br><br>Lead end-to-end data science projects focused on IT operations, incident management, and experience optimization.<br>Analyze structured and unstructured data from ITSM systems (e.g., ServiceNow), endpoint telemetry platforms (e.g., Nexthink, Intune), and infrastructure monitoring tools.<br>Develop predictive models for incident forecasting, root cause analysis, and proactive remediation.<br>Design anomaly detection algorithms to identify performance degradation, user friction, or compliance risks.<br>Build dashboards and visualizations to communicate insights to technical and executive stakeholders.<br>Collaborate with IT architects, service owners, and automation teams to embed intelligence into operational workflows.<br>Evaluate data quality, lineage, and governance across diverse IT data sources.<br>Stay current with emerging trends in AIOps, DEX, and IT analytics.<br><br>Required Skills &amp; Experience:<br><br>Overall 15+ years of experience in IT &amp; Software, 8+ years of experience in data science, with at least 3 years focused on IT operations or enterprise IT analytics.<br>Proficiency in Python, SQL, and data science libraries (e.g., scikit-learn, pandas, TensorFlow).<br>Strong understanding of ITSM data structures, incident lifecycle, and operational KPIs.<br>Experience with telemetry platforms (e.g., Nexthink, SysTrack, Intune, SCCM) and endpoint data.<br>Familiarity with cloud infrastructure metrics (Azure, AWS, GCP) and log analytics.<br>Expertise in statistical modeling, machine learning, and time-series analysis.<br>Ability to work independently and manage multiple complex projects simultaneously.<br>Expertise in using compute and AI resources on MS Azure.<br>Expertise in using statistical un-supervised models, supervised models, LLMs and SLMs<br>Excellent communication skills for cross-functional collaboration and executive reporting.<br><br>Preferred Qualifications:<br><br>Experience in AIOps, DEX, or EUC analytics domains.<br>Knowledge of ServiceNow, performance analytics, and integration workflows.<br>Exposure to MLOps frameworks and model deployment in enterprise environments.<br>Advanced degree in Computer Science, Statistics, or a related field.<br><br>Here at Atos, diversity and inclusion are embedded in our DNA. Read more about our commitment to a fair work environment for all.<br><br>Atos is a recognized leader in its industry across Environment, Social and Governance (ESG) criteria. Find out more on our CSR commitment.<br><br>Choose your future. Choose Atos. .</span></div><div jsname="G7vtgf" class="TOQyFc Uzkg7d MmMIvd brKmxb" aria-controls="tsuid_INP6aqDbJqqQ4-EPq6ieeQ_222" role="button" tabindex="0" jsaction="EMtXr" data-l="" data-hveid="CCwQRQ" data-ved="2ahUKEwig67LAnIyYAxUqyDgGHSuUJw8Ql5ACegQILBBF"><hr class="Bi9oQd" aria-hidden="true"><div class="Wjtive btku5b rXoM2c sjVJQd"><div class="niO4u VDgVie SlP8xc"><span class="cHaqb"><span class="PBBEhf">Show full description</span></span><span class="T2xY9b w2fKdd z1asCe" aria-hidden="true" style="height:18px;line-height:18px;width:18px"><svg focusable="false" aria-hidden="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 -960 960 960"><path d="M480-344L240-584l56-56L480-456L664-640l56,56L480-344Z"></path></svg></span></div></div></div></div></div><div class="XFOJCe" data-ved="2ahUKEwig67LAnIyYAxUqyDgGHSuUJw8Q5ZkFegQILBBG"><div class="EyBRub" data-ved="2ahUKEwig67LAnIyYAxUqyDgGHSuUJw8Qyo8CegQILBBH"><div jscontroller="Wo3n8" jsname="aadvhe" jsmodel=" d5EhJe" data-bkt="horizon_jobs" data-fhs="" data-maindata='[null,null,"bind(&#39;java/com/google/gws/plugins/horizon/jobs/viewer/herocontent/jslayout/feedback_messages.html#JobAtEmployer&#39;,{employ